{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3244","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3244","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3244\",\"parent_revision\":\"45fa7325a72943e4cca712c45e1bbc47356765f7\",\"root_revision\":\"9eb1f6bcbedece679af97aa170e63afaf253675f05e2d89f28aa863cb7deb0d1\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-27\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nprocess-siren (plugin-creator:process-siren agent / process-siren:woo-sailor skill) produces Mermaid diagrams inline in the target file under a fidelity mandate \u2014 one node per prose step/condition/outcome, nothing merged or omitted. When the target is a skill's SKILL.md, a large diagram can push the file's token count over skilllint's SK006/AS005 threshold (4400 tokens), triggering a warning that must then be resolved by hand.\\n\\nObserved: running woo-sailor's full-step-fidelity rebuild against plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md's Dispatch Flow diagram (PR #3243) pushed the file from 4306 to 4977 tokens, over the threshold. A separate follow-up agent then had to manually relocate the diagram to a references/dispatch-flow.md file behind a context pointer to clear the warning \u2014 this repo's existing progressive-disclosure convention (mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents) already supports this pattern, and references/acceptance-test-guide.md in the same skill is a working precedent.\\n\\nprocess-siren should make this decision itself instead of requiring a manual follow-up every time: when a diagram it produces is reference/verification material that some execution paths don't need (information-hierarchy tier 3), and inlining it would push the target file over the token-budget threshold, it should extract the diagram to a disclosed reference file reached by a context pointer, rather than always inlining. When a diagram is load-bearing content every execution path needs (information-hierarchy tier 1), it should stay inline regardless of size \u2014 a blanket always-extract-when-large rule would incorrectly push genuinely load-bearing diagrams behind a pointer that every invocation needs to see immediately.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: Tie the extraction threshold to skilllint's own 4400-token SK006/AS005 line (or a diagram-specific line count). Update the plugin-creator:process-siren agent definition and/or the process-siren:woo-sailor skill's dispatch logic to make this decision automatically. The extracted file should follow the existing references/*.md + context-pointer pattern already used elsewhere in this repo, not a bare .mmd/.mermaid file.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-27T01:46:27.896852Z</sub>\\n\\n### Verification Summary\\n\\nAll factual claims verified against primary sources (tooling output, source code, git history, direct command execution). Zero refutations; all load-bearing claims for the item's premise are confirmed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 1: PR #3243 token count change (Description)\\n**Claim:** \\\"running woo-sailor...pushed the file from 4306 to 4977 tokens\\\"\\n\\n**Verification:**\\n- Before PR #3243 (commit 15a902dc6): 4306 tokens \u2014 confirmed via `uvx skilllint@latest check --tokens-only` against historical file\\n- After PR #3243 (commit 6d332b509): 4977 tokens \u2014 confirmed via `uvx skilllint@latest check --tokens-only` against PR commit\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 2: references/acceptance-test-guide.md precedent (Description)\\n**Claim:** \\\"references/acceptance-test-guide.md in the same skill is a working precedent\\\"\\n\\n**Verification:**\\n- File exists at `/plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/references/acceptance-test-guide.md` (6.2k)\\n- Follows pattern: `.md` file behind a context pointer in parent SKILL.md\\n- Later evidence: PR #3245 (commit dcb192564) extracted the Dispatch Flow diagram to the same directory as `dispatch-flow.md` (5.5k), proving this pattern is the repository convention for diagram disclosure\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 3: skilllint constants programmatically available (Research, Wave 0)\\n**Claim:** \\\"uvx --from skilllint python -c ... print(BODY_TOKEN_WARNING)\\\" prints 4400, and BODY_TOKEN_ERROR is 8800\\n\\n**Verification:**\\n```bash\\nuvx --from skilllint python -c \\\\\\n  \\\"from skilllint.limits import BODY_TOKEN_WARNING, BODY_TOKEN_ERROR; \\\\\\n   print(f'WARNING: {BODY_TOKEN_WARNING}, ERROR: {BODY_TOKEN_ERROR}')\\\"\\n```\\nOutput: `WARNING: 4400, ERROR: 8800`\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 4: process-siren.md Step 6 unconditional (Research, Wave 0)\\n**Claim:** \\\"Step 6 ('Replace or Return') is binary and unconditional: there is no size check, no token-count check, and no branch that ever writes the diagram to a separate `references/*.md` file\\\"\\n\\n**Verification:**\\nSource: `plugins/process-siren/agents/process-siren.md`, lines 217\u2013220\\n\\n> ### Step 6: Replace or Return\\n> - If operating on a file: replace the original content with the diagram using Edit\\n> - If called standalone: return the Mermaid source in a fenced code block with `mermaid` language specifier\\n\\nNo conditional logic for size, token count, or file-placement decision. No reference to `references/` extraction. No step 6b or branching logic.\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 5: woo-sailor/SKILL.md has no diagram-placement logic (Research, Wave 0)\\n**Claim:** \\\"woo-sailor/SKILL.md is a pure dispatch/argument-routing skill...zero diagram-placement or duplication logic\\\"\\n\\n**Verification:**\\nSource: `plugins/process-siren/skills/woo-sailor/SKILL.md` (full file read)\\n\\nSkill description (line 3): \\\"...converts prose/bullet workflows to Mermaid diagrams \u2014 **delegates to the process-siren:process-siren agent**.\\\"\\n\\nFrontmatter (line 7): `agent: process-siren:process-siren`\\n\\nMermaid workflow (lines 22\u201343): Routes files to the agent via `Agent(subagent_type='process-siren:process-siren', prompt=...)` with either dry-run or live mode. No diagram-placement or duplication detection steps. No size/token thresholds checked. No branching for reference file extraction.\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Claim 6: No duplication-detection tooling exists (Research, Wave 0)\\n**Claim:** \\\"No existing skilllint/markdownlint tooling detects 'prose and diagram describe the same content' duplication\\\"\\n\\n**Verification:**\\n\\n**skilllint rules search:**\\n```bash\\nuvx skilllint@latest rules | grep -i \\\"dupl\\\\|redund\\\\|overlap\\\"\\n```\\nResult: No output \u2014 no matching rules.\\n\\n**markdownlint configuration:**\\nSource: `.markdownlint-cli2.jsonc`\\n- MD024 (duplicate headings) is explicitly disabled (line 13): `\\\"MD024\\\": false`\\n- All active rules are markdown *structure* checks (spacing, formatting, syntax), not semantic content checks\\n- No rule for \\\"this paragraph says the same thing as that diagram\\\"\\n\\n**Conclusion:**\\n- skilllint: no semantic content-duplication rules in any rule family\\n- markdownlint: only structural duplicate-heading detection (which is disabled); no semantic overlap detection\\n- Any duplication-avoidance logic for process-siren would need to be built from scratch\\n\\n**Verdict:** VERIFIED\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Overall Assessment\\n\\nAll factual claims in backlog item #3244 (Description and Wave 0 Research sections) are confirmed against primary sources. No claims are refuted. The premise of the item \u2014 that PR #3243 demonstrated a real problem (token-count overflow), and that precedent exists for the solution (references/ disclosure pattern) \u2014 is sound. The characterization of current process-siren behavior (unconditional inlining, no size check, no duplication detection) is accurate.\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-27T01:36:09.6997