ocess-siren's file-creation mode, per the-rewrite-room contract preservation)\\n</div>\\n\\n## Files\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-27T05:21:27.102003Z</sub>\\n\\n- `plugins/process-siren/agents/process-siren.md` \u2014 Step 6 (\\\"Replace or Return\\\", line 217) and Step 7 (\\\"Annotate the Replacement\\\", line 222) define today's unconditional-inline behavior; this is the primary file whose behavior this item concerns.\\n- `plugins/process-siren/skills/woo-sailor/SKILL.md` \u2014 pure dispatch/routing skill with no placement logic of its own; its description and behavior summary should stay accurate once process-siren's contract changes.\\n- `plugins/process-siren/README.md` \u2014 currently silent on placement behavior; should document the new conditional behavior once it exists.\\n- `plugins/the-rewrite-room/agents/rewrite-room-doc-converter.md` and `plugins/the-rewrite-room/skills/user-docs-to-ai-skill/{SKILL.md,references/workflow-identification.md,references/quality-criteria.md}` \u2014 the only confirmed in-repo consumers of process-siren's output; their file-creation-mode contract (diagram is the sole file content) must remain intact.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/SKILL.md` and its `references/dispatch-flow.md` \u2014 the concrete instance that surfaced this item (PRs #3240, #3241, #3243, #3245, #3247); not itself in scope to retrofit here (see Dependencies).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Resources\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-27T05:21:27.102019Z</sub>\\n\\n- `mattpocock-skills:writing-for-agents` skill \u2014 progressive-disclosure and duplication-avoidance principles this item is grounded in.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/references/acceptance-test-guide.md` \u2014 working precedent for the references/*.md + context-pointer pattern.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/multi-perspective-review/references/dispatch-flow.md` \u2014 working precedent for a disclosed diagram specifically (extracted in PR #3245).\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` routing sections \u2014 working precedent for diagram-only content with zero parallel prose.\\n- skilllint `limits.py` (external checkout, `/Users/jamienelson/repos/skilllint/packages/skilllint/limits.py`) \u2014 source of truth for `BODY_TOKEN_WARNING = 4400` / `BODY_TOKEN_ERROR = 8800`, queryable at runtime via `uvx --from skilllint python -c \\\"from skilllint.limits import BODY_TOKEN_WARNING; print(BODY_TOKEN_WARNING)\\\"`.\\n- `plugins/the-rewrite-room/skills/user-docs-to-ai-skill/references/workflow-identification.md` (line 154) \u2014 states the file-creation-mode contract this item must not break: \\\"the diagram is the artifact \u2014 no additional content is needed.\\\"\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-27T05:21:27.101928Z</sub>\\n\\nAffects every future invocation of `plugin-creator:process-siren` (agent) or `process-siren:woo-sailor` (skill) that inserts or updates a diagram inside an existing multi-section document \u2014 the primary confirmed path is skill/agent/CLAUDE.md authoring and revision work in this repo. Confirmed downstream consumer: the-rewrite-room's `user-docs-to-ai-skill` pipeline (`rewrite-room-doc-converter.md`, `user-docs-to-ai-skill/SKILL.md`, `references/workflow-identification.md`, `references/quality-criteria.md`) delegates to process-siren for freshly-created single-diagram files at `resources/workflows/{slug}.md` and depends on the current unconditional-inline contract for that file-creation case \u2014 this item's fix must not alter behavior for that consumer. Repo-wide grep confirmed these are the only in-repo callers of `process-siren:process-siren` or `process-siren:woo-sailor`. No CI workflow, test suite, or automated gate currently exercises process-siren's placement behavior, so a regression here would surface only through the same kind of manual discovery that produced this item.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Impact Radius\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-27T01:45:23.594069Z</sub>\\n\\nSCOPE_EXPANSION: Wave 0 research named process-siren.md, woo-sailor/SKILL.md, and skilllint's threshold as starting points. This pass adds one consumer not previously named: the-rewrite-room plugin's `user-docs-to-ai-skill` pipeline, which delegates to `process-siren:process-siren` and hard-codes an assumption (\\\"the diagram is the artifact \u2014 no additional content is needed\\\") that the fix's disclosure logic could break for freshly-created single-diagram output files. Also confirms `process-siren.md`'s `tools:` grant (Read, Write, Edit, Grep, Glob, Bash) already covers everything the fix needs \u2014 no frontmatter tool-grant gap.\\n\\n## Systems Inventory\\n\\n| System | Path | Category | Relationship |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| process-siren agent | `plugins/process-siren/agents/process-siren.md` | Code \u2014 Producer | Primary edit target: Step 6 \\\"Replace or Return\\\" (line 217) and Step 7 \\\"Annotate the Replacement\\\" (line 222) define today's unconditional-inline behavior |\\n| woo-sailor skill | `plugins/process-siren/skills/woo-sailor/SKILL.md` | Code \u2014 Producer | Bulk-conversion dispatcher; spawns `process-siren:process-siren` per file \u2014 pure routing, no placement logic of its own (confirmed Wave 0) |\\n| improve-processes skill | `plugins/process-siren/skills/improve-processes/SKILL.md` | Code \u2014 Producer | Loaded by process-siren.md (frontmatter `skills:`) as a pre-conversion quality gate; governs source readiness, not diagram placement |\\n| mermaids-treasure skill | `plugins/process-siren/skills/mermaids-treasure/SKILL.md` + `references/*.md` | Code \u2014 Producer | Loaded by process-siren.md (frontmatter `skills:`) as Mermaid syntax reference; unaffected by placement logic |\\n| rewrite-room-doc-converter agent | `plugins/the-rewrite-room/agents/rewrite-room-doc-converter.md` | Code \u2014 Consumer | Delegates Phase 1.5 to `process-siren:process-siren` via Task (line 33); its own Mermaid flowchart docu